 "notes": "Level = the province (sigla) written after the town, e.g. \"20121 Milano MI\". ISO codes are IT-<sigla> except Valle d'Aosta: ISO has no province code there, only the region IT-23, so IT-23 is used (sigla AO; our old key IT-AO is an alias). Sardinia (LR 7/2021, DGR 36/34 of 9 Jul 2025, BURAS 17 Jul 2025): metropolitan cities Cagliari (CA) and Sassari (SS), provinces Nuoro (NU), Oristano (OR), Gallura Nord-Est Sardegna, Ogliastra, Medio Campidano, Sulcis Iglesiente; Sud Sardegna abolished. ISO 3166-2:IT has not been updated: it still has IT-SU Sud Sardegna and no codes for the 4 new provinces, and their former ISO codes IT-OT/IT-OG/IT-VS/IT-CI (deleted 2019) and IT-SD (corrected to IT-SU 2020) must not be reused, so the 4 new provinces get CC-NAME codes. Sigle: ISTAT (Feb 2026 list) OT, OG, VS, CI; DPR 4 Aug 2026 n.183 (GU n.238, 13 Oct 2026) sets plates OT, OG, VS and gives SU to Sulcis Iglesiente. So IT-SU (Sud Sardegna, capital Carbonia) is mapped forward to Sulcis Iglesiente (capital Carbonia, now sigla SU); parts of old Sud Sardegna are now in Medio Campidano and the Cagliari metropolitan city, so that alias is approximate. IT-SS now covers the smaller Sassari metropolitan city (Gallura split off). Low confidence: sigla for Sulcis Iglesiente (CI vs SU) and Poste Italiane usage not confirmed."
}
